@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Help and About"; }
<div class="cc-grid"><section class="cc-card"><h2 class="text-success">CropCare</h2><p>IoT-based soil monitoring and fertilizer decision support for corn farmers.</p><p class="text-muted">Version @(typeof(CropCare.Web.Models.CropCareProfile).Assembly.GetName().Version?.ToString(3) ?? "1.0.0")</p><h3>Getting started</h3><ol><li>Create a farm zone with its area and planting date.</li><li>Scan or upload the provisioned sensor QR, name it and select its zone.</li><li>Review actual measurements, their timestamps and recorded history.</li><li>Mark a crop harvested, then select a new planting date for the next cycle.</li></ol><p>Recent readings indicate recent measurements, not guaranteed device connectivity. No measurements means no recorded data—not zero soil nutrients.</p></section><section class="cc-card"><h2>Developer Team</h2><p>Kevin John Pama</p><p>Jason Chris Lim</p><p>Job Edward Yakit</p><p>John Dhenzell Ermac</p><h3>Troubleshooting</h3><p>For missing readings, check the device's power and network, then refresh. Allow camera access on HTTPS or upload a QR image instead.</p><p>Use Forgot Password to request an email code. Subscription references are reviewed manually; never enter a PIN or OTP.</p><p class="text-muted">For additional assistance, contact your CropCare project team.</p></section></div>
